.TH LLM-MANAGER-HELPER 8 "2026-08-29" "LLM-Manager" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
llm-manager-helper \- apply an approved LLM-Manager system setting request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llm-manager-helper
.I operation-id request-sha256
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llm-manager-helper
is the restricted privileged boundary used by LLM-Manager. It accepts only an
operation identifier and a canonical request hash. Requests, staged content,
paths, operations, metadata, expiry, and before hashes are validated internally.
.PP
This command is intended to be launched by the installed PolicyKit action or by
the documented remote sudo flow. It does not accept shell commands, arbitrary
arguments, or caller-provided target paths.
.PP
Local ATOMIC_REPLACE requests require the independently resolved local hostname,
complete workflow bindings, and explicitly initialized root backup storage.
The helper captures the original fixed target into encrypted root-owned evidence
under the same target lock before writing. Missing keys, capture failure, stale
targets, or expiry prevent the write. Setup is never performed automatically.
Existing rollback operations do not recapture the target.
.PP
The target lock spans capture, the write and declared service operations for one
request. It does not span later external validation or a separate rollback request.
See llm-manager-restore-setup(8) for administrator initialization.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.nbe03xxx.llm-manager.policy
PolicyKit action for local system setting changes.
.TP
.I /var/lib/llm-manager/helper-receipts
Root-only replay receipts.
.SH SECURITY
Do not copy or replace this executable outside the package manager. LLM-Manager
must remain unprivileged; only this helper is elevated for an approved request.
